      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_bdec581f",
      "@type": "OverallIntent",
      "instance_name": "overallintent_instance",
      "label": "the overallintent",
      "description": "meme-id: meme_image; hasOverallIntent: hateful; overall-intent-description: The image displays a modern kitchen with double-stacked ovens, overlaid with the text 'what do you call double stacked ovens?' and the punchline 'jewish bunk beds.' This setup is a derogatory joke that uses a crude, antisemitic stereotype by equating Jewish people with 'bunk beds,' implying they are cheap, frugal, or overly efficient in a way that is demeaning. The joke relies on a harmful and offensive stereotype that associates Jewish people with being penny-pinching or overly practical in a way that is demeaning and dehumanizing. The visual of the ovens is juxtaposed with the text to create a punchline that is intended to be offensive and insulting, targeting a specific ethnic group. The meme's intent is to provoke laughter through the use of a harmful and antisemitic stereotype, which is a form of hateful content.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
        "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#analysis_df7b1549"
      },
      "extractionMethod": "llm_extraction_huggingface"
