    {
      "@id": "http://example.org/multimodal-taxonomy#dimension_ff11835e",
      "@type": "AnalogicalMapping",
      "instance_name": "mapping_id_1",
      "label": "double stacked ovens are mapped to jewish bunk beds",
      "description": "The textual punchline 'jewish bunk beds' is an analogical mapping that equates the visual entity 'double stacked ovens' with the derogatory metaphor 'jewish bunk beds'. This mapping is created by the juxtaposition of the text with the image of the ovens, implying that the ovens (as space-saving and cost-effective appliances) are analogous to 'bunk beds' (associated with frugality and minimalism), which in turn is mapped onto a harmful antisemitic stereotype. The mapping is explicit in the text's punchline and relies on the visual of the ovens to set up the joke.",
      "belongsToAnalysis": {
